{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel","id":1547262,"title":"Can mages time travel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-26T11:18:25-08:00","id":1547262,"title":"Can mages time travel?","content":"Considering that some beings in Mage such as the Zigg'raugglurr can do so, can Mages do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-26-2024, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T12:01:04-08:00","id":1547263,"title":"","content":"There are exceedingly few things in Mage that are a hard &quot;no&quot; in terms of what they can do. Time travel is, however, risky, difficulty, and so on, in a fashion that leads the majority of mages to avoid it. Basically, the game wants to keep time travel from taking over the game once one PC can do it; unless you basically want to go full on &quot;lost in time&quot; as a game premise. Since most mages would rather not explode from Paradox or get stuck blindly jumping around time hoping they can find where they started before they're stuck in a collapsing time-branch... most mages consider time travel a fairly &quot;weapon of last resort&quot; to do with hung/conditional spell to rewind a scene or something of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T13:53:17-08:00","id":1547267,"title":"","content":"The simple answer is yes, but it's probably the most perilous working a mage can try to perform.<br /> <br /> Aside from most forms of time travel raking in potentially enormous amounts of Paradox, it's a practice which attracts the attention of other people and entities (even aside from Paradox spirits) who are capable of sensing or detecting such anomalies in the tapestry, and in many cases that attention can make even most sorts of Paradox backlash seem trivial by comparison. A mage would do very well to remember that they are not the only one capable of meddling with time and the course of events, and that some of those other parties are powers which no sane willworker would ever want to come face to face with.<br /> <br /> A long time ago, I would routinely sic Wrinkle on characters who made use of Time effects I found troublesome or inconvenient to plots and storylines. I fully recognize how immature and petulant that was, and I still cringle a bit over it. That was also very sloppy thinking on my part, as I simply hadn't thought the matter through. Like &quot;game breaking&quot; uses of Correspondence, there are much more logical and reasonable ways of explaining why mages rarely try to meddle with history. I simply learned to think ahead and consider that events important to extremely powerful parties are inevitably guarded or watched over by those parties, in the same way that places important to those of sufficient power are warded/guarded/monitored against snooping by seers, and that need not involve any capricious use of Storyteller fait. Does this mean it's not possible for a mage to get away with that sort of intrusion? No, but it does mean such a mage is taking an enormous risk in some cases, and needs to tread <i>very </i>carefully. In some instances, it's just not worth that risk.<br /> <br /> This is largely anthropic reasoning. In theory, could a mage look back in time and try to discover the truth about Caine? Yes. Why hasn't anyone ever done it, or revealed what they discovered if they did? Think about it a moment. There are things out there which are going to take notice if someone even <i>peeks </i>into certain events, let alone puts themselves into a position to alter them. Depending on what one attracts the notice <i>of</i>, the results could range from troublesome to the sort of thing one ought not even whisper of. While there are ways of reducing the risk of that, there are some &quot;places&quot; the wise do not tread.<br /> <br /> That said, How Do You DO That contains some interesting advice on working with Time, including different sorts of time travel (there's more than one) and the possible benefits and consequences. As a bit of personal advice gained from long experience, characters being able to work with Time itself was very good incentive for me to develop skill at running non-linear storylines for Mage. Getting away from attempting to guide linear plots ironically saved me a countless headaches, once I got the hang of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T18:03:31-08:00","id":1547269,"title":"","content":"I see it this way. It's what you plan to do. If you want to prevent the Kennedy or Lincoln assassination, paradox will fry you hard. Everyone and everything will be transformed. Paradox will erase your very existence. <br /> <br /> However, there are other possibilities. Any mistakes while pursuing these possibilities will fry you as badly but it isn't a necessary outcome. It is a profoundly likely outcome, but not necessary.<br /> <br /> Say you go back to ancient Greece and gather up a few dozen high quality literary works that deal with the Greek myths and those of several nearby peoples whose mythologies were mainly lost. You place these scrolls and codices in a large jar which you seal up in a place that hasn't been touched by archeologists. If you play your cards right, you could bring forth an explosion of new interest in the culture of classical antiquity. Something any Hermetic would love to do. <br /> <br /> It would be a profoundly dangerous mission but, as it wouldn't change anyone's experience of the past, it shouldn't invoke paradox. <br /> <br /> Any trip to the past would have to be insanely careful not to change anyone's experience of the past. That's anyone no matter how obscure or unimportant to others. It is a desperately difficult standard. Which is why time travel is avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T18:07:17-08:00","id":1547271,"title":"","content":"What if you steal a book from the Library of Alexandria before it got burned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-26T21:05:51-08:00","id":1547272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547271#post1547271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you steal a book from the Library of Alexandria before it got burned?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good example of what I was speaking of previously. The Library of Alexandria was an important resource to the Order of Hermes and the Ahl-i-Batin, as well as the site of a Node which became a lynchpin of Horizon's creation. They did manage to preserve much of the important work there, unbeknownst to Sleepers (and probably most mages.) Attempting to meddle with it in any way whatsoever would be an <i>incredibly bad idea</i>. I can't imagine the place not being protected by some very powerful wards set up to prevent all manner of meddling, but even if you managed to circumvent them it would undoubtedly immediately grab the attention of a historical Porthos, or someone even less likely to simply warn you away sternly from what you're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-27-2024, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T05:56:36-08:00","id":1547273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547271#post1547271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you steal a book from the Library of Alexandria before it got burned?</div> </div> </div> </div>A far more practical idea would be to go to the library to BUY a book. They sold copies. Mind you all the evidence is that the library was in serious decay well before Cleopatra was born. Still, being a quiet little nobody and buying a cheap copy of the desired text could work, but only if you are fanatically careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T07:11:16-08:00","id":1547274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547271#post1547271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you steal a book from the Library of Alexandria before it got burned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im a fan of Novicows self consistency principle. If youre going to the past that means you already did. Maybe your break in for the book caused the library to burn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T11:39:59-08:00","id":1547279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547273#post1547273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A far more practical idea would be to go to the library to BUY a book. They sold copies. Mind you all the evidence is that the library was in serious decay well before Cleopatra was born. Still, being a quiet little nobody and buying a cheap copy of the desired text could work, but only if you are fanatically careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a somewhat safer option would be to scry into the past for the particular volume you want, then use a secondary effect to create a duplicate in the present. Hermetics have a very interesting rote which transcribes a person's surface thoughts into a blank book, so with the appropriate effects I imagine it'd be possible to reproduce the contents of a volume in a similar way.<br /> <br /> Granted, this is almost certainly going to be noticed by those associated with the Library of Alexandria at the time, but with some serious luck they <i>might </i>pause to examine exactly what it is you're trying to do, and <i>might </i>even appreciate the effort and method. I have this really humorous mental image of a mage failing in an attempt at this, only to have the actual volume they were trying to copy delivered to them shortly thereafter along with an eccentrically worded note written by Porthos, when he's already perished in the present time. (This should <i>still </i>make a person very nervous, if they know much at all about Porthos..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T13:14:58-08:00","id":1547283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547269#post1547269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it this way. It's what you plan to do. If you want to prevent the Kennedy or Lincoln assassination, paradox will fry you hard. Everyone and everything will be transformed. Paradox will erase your very existence.<br /> <br /> However, there are other possibilities. Any mistakes while pursuing these possibilities will fry you as badly but it isn't a necessary outcome. It is a profoundly likely outcome, but not necessary.<br /> <br /> Say you go back to ancient Greece and gather up a few dozen high quality literary works that deal with the Greek myths and those of several nearby peoples whose mythologies were mainly lost. You place these scrolls and codices in a large jar which you seal up in a place that hasn't been touched by archeologists. If you play your cards right, you could bring forth an explosion of new interest in the culture of classical antiquity. Something any Hermetic would love to do.<br /> <br /> It would be a profoundly dangerous mission but, as it wouldn't change anyone's experience of the past, it shouldn't invoke paradox.<br /> <br /> Any trip to the past would have to be insanely careful not to change anyone's experience of the past. That's anyone no matter how obscure or unimportant to others. It is a desperately difficult standard. Which is why time travel is avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I think the above is one approach to time travel and it's fairly constricting becasue it makes past events immutable and thus cause paradox, but it's not the only option, if you wanted to make time travel a part of your campaign then you could examine the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TimeTravel\" target=\"_blank\">various tropes</a> and decide on how you want to allow/penalise time travel as there are many options for <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TemporalMutability\" target=\"_blank\">Temporal Mutability</a>.<br /> <br /> Immutable - you can't alter past events and if you try Paradox burns you badly<br /> Butterfly - past events are readily alterable but tend to have huge changes on the 'now'<br /> Deterministic - history tends to fall into a pattern, you can murder baby hitler but someone just as bad ends up filling the same space<br /> Timelines - any change in the past puts you onto a new timeline<br /> Multiverse - many different timelines exist at once and time travel is more like switching between different dimensions<br /> Quantum Leap - changing past events can gradually improve the 'now'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T14:32:11-08:00","id":1547286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547283#post1547283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm, I think the above is one approach to time travel and it's fairly constricting becasue it makes past events immutable and thus cause paradox, but it's not the only option, if you wanted to make time travel a part of your campaign then you could examine the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TimeTravel\" target=\"_blank\">various tropes</a> and decide on how you want to allow/penalise time travel as there are many options for <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TemporalMutability\" target=\"_blank\">Temporal Mutability</a>.<br /> <br /> Immutable - you can't alter past events and if you try Paradox burns you badly<br /> Butterfly - past events are readily alterable but tend to have huge changes on the 'now'<br /> Deterministic - history tends to fall into a pattern, you can murder baby hitler but someone just as bad ends up filling the same space<br /> Timelines - any change in the past puts you onto a new timeline<br /> Multiverse - many different timelines exist at once and time travel is more like switching between different dimensions<br /> Quantum Leap - changing past events can gradually improve the 'now'<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Multiverse option is one Etherites have played around with quite a bit. The Quantum Temporal Travel rote can be found in the Tradition Book: Sons of Ether (Revised,) and within the Enlightened Grimoire in a form updated for M20. The former also has some good advice for handling instances in which characters might travel to alternate universes, which isn't time travel in the <i>strictest </i>sense, but is a wonderfully Etherite thing to be doing.<br /> <br /> However, it would be well to keep in mind that some powers and entities would very likely take notice of trespassers from alternate realities, and depending on where and when such a voyager is trespassing they may react no more kindly to it than the residents of their home reality would. Some of them may even have some means of following you back. There are a couple interesting movies dealing with that sort of possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-28-2024, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T14:33:13-08:00","id":1547287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547274#post1547274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im a fan of Novicows self consistency principle. If youre going to the past that means you already did.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly how Novikov's self-consistency principle works. That's a result of the principle in broad application. The only requirement of self-consistency is that anything a time-traveler does can't cause a temporal paradox. The MCU Loki show actually demonstrates one of the proposed ways to do stuff in the past of the time-stream without violating self-consistency: go to a place and time where nothing you do matters because a natural disaster is going to so thoroughly destroy the area that no evidence remains. The past remains self-consistent, even if superficially altered; and whether you did or didn't already do something because of time-travel is unresolved until you actually do it.<br /> <br /> There are problems, such as the fact that inevitably multiple people are going to have the same idea and such spots would become unstable due to tragedy of the commons on a temporal resources scale.<br /> <br /> There are also benefits because the bigger the disaster the more you can get away with: you could build the most impressive supercomputer ever, put it in the path of a planet killer asteroid ala the one that killed off the dinosaurs, and in the present be able to perform immense computations virtually instantly from the perspective of people around you in the &quot;now.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547283#post1547283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I think the above is one approach to time travel and it's fairly constricting becasue it makes past events immutable and thus cause paradox, but it's not the only option, if you wanted to make time travel a part of your campaign then you could examine the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TimeTravel\" target=\"_blank\">various tropes</a> and decide on how you want to allow/penalise time travel as there are many options for <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TemporalMutability\" target=\"_blank\">Temporal Mutability</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default present in the books doesn't quite fit any of these, because the point of being a mage is that you can to give the laws of physics a middle finger.<br /> <br /> One of the ways the WoD differs from the real world, is the Umbra. In effect, the past (now at least) is immutable, and changes are shunted into the Umbra instead depending on their nature. The Astral Realms are, in theory, full of potential histories that didn't happen. It's closest to the multiverse approach, but it isn't actually a multiverse; just the one universe that has very weird rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T01:37:09-08:00","id":1547362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547287#post1547287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the ways the WoD differs from the real world, is the Umbra. In effect, the past (now at least) is immutable, and changes are shunted into the Umbra instead depending on their nature. The Astral Realms are, in theory, full of potential histories that didn't happen. It's closest to the multiverse approach, but it isn't actually a multiverse; just the one universe that has very weird rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you and Steve are missing my point, it's not about what the lore and the books say, it's about what kind of story you'd like to tell at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T03:47:56-08:00","id":1547368,"title":"","content":"Alternately, you're missing the point that the distinction your drawing isn't really necessary. If you want to run a game with some form of temporal mutability, but want to use Mage, there are options to get away from the default presumption of an immutable past enforced by strong Paradox. Weird Ether Science! and traveling to Realms where the impact of time travel shenanigans are allowed to unfold are tools to get to a specific type of story without having to circumvent the lore and books to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-31T22:14:16-08:00","id":1547409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1547262-can-mages-time-travel?p=1547362#post1547362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you and Steve are missing my point, it's not about what the lore and the books say, it's about what kind of story you'd like to tell at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I've been attempting to do is to point out parts of the source material which usefully deal with what's being discussed, which is the most constructive sort of input/answer I can give.<br /> <br /> While the group I play with refrains from &quot;house ruling&quot; anything unless we <i>must</i>, because it's something entirely unaddressed by the creators of the game, I certainly do realize that other players and Storytellers will end up doing that to match their own tastes. (This is not for the sake of dogmatism on our part, it's because we're a group of grey TTRPGers who've been running chronicles lasting well over a decade, and sticking that close to the source material helps us remain consistent over such a stretch.)<br /> <br /> If the feeling is that I'm trying to tell anyone how to run their game, that doesn't seem to be something I could do even if I cared to try. I've got my hands plenty full as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 01-01-2025, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}